Job Description:
KEY PERFORMANCE AREAS
Customer Relations and Service Delivery
Provincial linkages and participation (Career Expo's; Job Faires; and Industry Related Expo's);
Represent TETA in Mpumalanga meetings, forums, etc at the Provincial level as and when delegated or required and handle queries of Municipal Training Committees;
Responsible for providing support to TETA (chamber) stakeholder and provide excellent, professional services;
Attend to contract related queries from stakeholders within time frame;
Timeously respond to Ad Hoc telephonic and electronic queries from stakeholders (internal & external);
Respond to queries via emails and telephonically;
Consultation with stakeholders;
Keep up to date about what is being communicated to stakeholders on the website and other forms of media;
Attend and participate in Annual workshops targeting SDFs & relevant stakeholders;
Advise and assist stakeholders accordingly when enquired about any marketing and media communications that was send out by TETA;
Provide Support to TETA corporate activity with assisting with Chamber Committee Meeting packs, arrangement;
Attend and participate in annual workshops targeting SDFs and relevant stakeholders.
Finance and Chamber Administration
Record, prepare and submit payment requisitions/claims for payment and provide proof of payments to stakeholders;
Upload claim documents on Sharepoint and Papertrail;
Assist with the coordination of travel arrangements for the chamber and Chamber Committee members;
Assist with processing of Subsistence, Travel and Chamber Committee allowance claims and submit to HR;
Provide personal assistance to the chamber Executive Officer timeously;
Assist with the arrangements and coordination of Chamber Committee meetings and minute-taking;
Keep an updated and accurate filing system of all chamber administrative documents;
Coordinate general procurement within the chamber in line with SCM processes;
Assist in addressing audit queries;
Assist in providing supporting documentation for DHET reporting;
Assist in collating information for monthly reporting to the office of the Chief Operations Officer.
DG Contract Administration
Assess DG claims;
Prepare evaluation reports and cheque requisition for payment;
Capture contract deliverables on QMS and Papertrail;
Capture learnership agreements on QMS and Papertrail;
Prepare addendum requests where amendments need to be effected on contracts;
Maintain an up-to-date filing system of all documentation in support of DG Claims;
Assist in generating DG contracts agreements and addendums once terms and conditions, deliverables and requirements has been finalised;
Upload new DG contracts on to the Papertrail;
Provide inputs to DG report and Commitment schedule;
Communicate contract deviations;
Maintain an updated registered SDF/Stakeholder database;
Conduct Project Monitoring and workplace approval visits;
Prepare the claim register weekly and send to finance monthly.
Implementation of MG
Verification of supporting documents and assisting the ETDP with MG assessment;
Conduct site inspection to monitor the implementation of WSP;
Advice stakeholders and EO of gaps identified;
Give recommendations where necessary to the stakeholders;
Stakeholder support on the TETA SMS system.
Provincial Office Management/Maintenance
Provincial Office building maintenance requirements reported;
Provincial Office facilities including cleaning and sanitation, gardening, safety and security, water, and electricity supported daily;
Provincial Office ICT equipment and infrastructure maintenance requirements reported;
Provincial Office assets, travel, stationery, catering, other requisitions and petty cash complied for approval in compliance with Finance requirements.
Mentoring and Coaching of Mpumalanga office staff
Train, coach and mentor staff;
Motivate interns to contribute and support team goals;
Manage staff time and attendance according to policy.
Requirements
MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS
Qualification and Experience
M + 3 in HRM/ETD relevant tertiary qualification;
At least 3 years administrative experience with exposure to ETD/SETA Environment, 1 year of which should be experience working with contracts and financial aspects thereof;
Exposure to SETA/Public sector environment will be an added Advantage;
Driver’ License is essential.

Detailed description
The successful candidate will be responsible for the following key performance areas:
Understanding institutions’ strategies and business models in the relevant environments to which the risk types relates;
monitoring the relevant industry’s exposure to the risk types;
monitoring industry compliance with regulations governing these risk types;
benchmarking an institution’s risk management practices with respect to the risk types management best practice;
evaluating an institution’s internal models for management of these risk types;
providing specialist input with regards to the risk types to front-line supervision and policy development;
developing analytical methods to analyse and interpret risk-based regulatory data submissions;
participating in capital/own fund requirement-adequacy assessments;
contributing to risk-based meetings with representatives of an institution and their auditors;
conducting thematic reviews pertaining to the risk types; and
informing the RSD of the aggregate behaviour of banks pertaining to the risk types.
Regulation
Developing and maintaining regulations and instructions governing statutory requirements for the risk types;
developing internal policies and processes for supervising the risk types; and
participating in international and domestic related forums in the establishment of regulations pertaining to the risk types.
Training
Ensuring widespread cognisance and understanding throughout the PA of the concepts and developments in the field of the risk types.
Job requirements
To be considered for this position, candidates must be in possession of:
a postgraduate degree (at least NQF level 8) in Finance, Banking, Economics, Mathematics, Statistics, Computer Science, Data Science, or another relevant quantitatively focused degree; preference will be given to candidates with financial mathematics or financial engineering post-graduate qualifications;
5-8 years applicable experience in the banking, insurance or financial regulatory sector in positions related to the risk types;
knowledge of, and experience in, the banking, insurance, and financial market infrastructure systems, financial products, regulations, and risk type approaches and models;
asset class experience across equities, FX, fixed income, etc;
thorough knowledge of the various standards developed by the international standard setting bodies related to the risk types at both a theoretical and practical level.
The following would be an added advantage:
Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA);
Financial Risk Manager (FRM) certification;
Certificate in Quantitative Finance (CQF) or another industry-recognised certification; and/or
Master of Business Administration (MBA) or another relevant Master’s-level (or higher) management-related qualification.
